      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شُجُبٌ</span></b>  <i>Three pieces of wood</i> [<i>set up as a tripod</i>]
<i>upon which the pastor hangs his bucket</i> (K, TA)
<i>and his skin for water or milk.</i> (TA.) [See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شِجَابٌ</span> (voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِشْجَبٌ</span>), of which it is said in the
